# Synthesis — HANKEL-03B / MEM-05 / CAL-05 / CHANNEL-05

The campaign separates four layers that had previously been easy to conflate.

1. **Composite rank evidence can be anytime-valid without determinant collapse.**  A checkpointed spectral test keeps `sigma_4`, reducing the worst practical scale from astronomical determinant bounds to tens of millions when two-step marginals are preverified.
2. **A broad rank-three process is genuinely close.**  The edge-emitting 3-state automaton raises the information-theoretic lower bound to roughly 0.26--0.54 million complete four-jump resets.  The remaining gap to the spectral certificate is statistical, but not all of the difficulty is statistical.
3. **Calibration structure matters.**  Paying the zero-row-sum constraint only where it is actually useful expands the certified primitive detector region by factors of several without changing the carrier theorem.
4. **Channel categories now have a finite fail-closed protocol.**  The protocol is conditional on an external dimensionless-time calibration and a simple common-efficiency detector model; no physical execution has occurred.

Current operational hierarchy:

`intrinsic carrier -> calibrated one-step carrier -> lower-order path checks -> composite rank/memory test -> channel-category test`.

None of these arrows supplies a physical platform, dimensional time, a universal memory law, or evidence that nature realizes FIN.
